# TruckSetu settings
#
# Copy this file to .env in this same folder, fill in what you want to use, and restart ./app.
# .env stays on your computer: git ignores it, because it holds passwords. Comments go on their own lines.
# Without a .env file everything still works: port 8080, no Google button, and the login codes are
# printed in the window where ./app runs instead of being emailed.

# --- Port ---
# PORT=8080

# --- "Continue with Google" ---
# 1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com and make a project (any name, e.g. TruckSetu).
# 2. Go to "Google Auth Platform" (APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen) and press Get started:
#    app name TruckSetu, your email as the support and contact email, audience External.
# 3. Clients > Create client > Web application. Under "Authorised JavaScript origins" add
#    http://localhost:8080 and http://localhost (no redirect URI is needed), then Create.
# 4. Audience: while the app is "Testing", only the Google accounts listed under Test users can sign in.
#    Add yours there, or press "Publish app" (plain sign-in with name and email needs no review).
# 5. Paste the client ID here. It ends with .apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Emailing the login codes ---
# With a Gmail account:
# 1. Turn on 2-Step Verification: https://myaccount.google.com/security
# 2. Make an app password at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (call it TruckSetu)
#    and paste its 16 letters as SMTP_PASSWORD. Never put your normal Gmail password here.
# 3. Fill in the four lines, for example:
#    SMTP_URL=smtps://smtp.gmail.com:465
#    SMTP_USER=yourname@gmail.com
#    SMTP_PASSWORD=abcdefghijklmnop
#    MAIL_FROM=TruckSetu <yourname@gmail.com>
# Any other mail service that gives SMTP details works the same way.
SMTP_URL=
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
# Who the codes come from; empty means SMTP_USER
MAIL_FROM=
